  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a dog lying on a bed using a laptop, with overlaid text that reads: 'what do you mean I've got a 30-day ban all i did was call him nigger.' The meme uses the dog as a visual metaphor for an innocent or unaware individual who has been punished for using a racially charged slur. The intent is to mock or trivialize the severity of racial slurs by framing the act as a minor offense deserving only a '30-day ban,' thereby implying that such language is not serious or harmful. This is a hateful meme because it normalizes and minimizes the use of a deeply offensive racial slur ('nigger'), which is a term historically and currently used to demean and dehumanize Black people. The juxtaposition of the dog's innocent appearance with the hateful text creates a false equivalence, suggesting that the offense is trivial, which is a form of indirect attack on Black people and their dignity. The meme's overall intent is to provoke laughter at the expense of racial injustice, thereby perpetuating harmful stereotypes and minimizing the gravity of racial violence and discrimination.",
